  "result": "Perfect! All 85 tests pass. I've added VAT calculations:\n\n**lineVAT(line)** \u2014 Calculates VAT per line:\n- VAT is computed on the line's amount **after discount**\n- Formula: `roundCents(lineAmount \u00d7 vatRate / 100)` where `lineAmount = lineTotal - lineDiscount`\n- Supports all three VAT rates: 21%, 9%, 0%\n\n**invoiceTotals** now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`:\n- `subtotal` = sum of all line totals (pre-discount)\n- `discount` = sum of all line discounts\n- `vat` = sum of all rounded line VATs (never a percentage of invoice total)\n- `total` = `subtotal - discount + vat` (clamped at 0)\n\n**renderInvoiceText** enhanced:\n- Shows VAT on its own line just above the total when vat > 0\n- Format: `VAT: \u20acnn.nn`\n- Example output:\n```\nINV-2026-0001\nNorthwind Studio\n2 \u00d7 Design work (hour) @ \u20ac85.00 = \u20ac170.00\nSubtotal: \u20ac170.00\nVAT: \u20ac35.70\nTotal: \u20ac205.70\n```\n\n**Key design decision:** VAT is computed **per line and rounded per line**, then summed for the invoice total \u2014 not calculated as a percentage of the invoice subtotal. This prevents rounding errors from accumulating.\n\n**Tests** (7 new) verify:\n- lineVAT calculations on amounts after discount\n- All VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n- Correct VAT formula in invoiceTotals\n- VAT shown in rendered output\n- VAT appears above total line\n- No VAT line when vat = 0",
